  "elements": [
    {
      "id": "oTRPM-P9rw0C9X-xhe5PB",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -3721.2826818462386,
      "y": 1924.6332563934693,
      "width": 941.2414698265428,
      "height": 532.3427129211375,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "a0",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 788070667,
      "version": 4659,
      "versionNonce": 68862629,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1792232494461,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "1. Functional Requirements :\n    1. Given a product, list down ranked \"n\" no. of products to the user that are frequently bought alongside or shortly after the target product\n    2. Ingest completed order events from the upstream order service without impacting checkout latency.\n    3. Similarity scoring : process the historical purchases and real time purchases and also eliminating the generic bestsellers (e.g., carry bags, milk etc.) so\nthat it doesn't dominate every page.\n    4. Real time post filtering : Before listing down the top list to client dynamically filter them lke out of stock, availability.\n    5. For newley launched product with zero -purchase history fall back to user already bought itmes.\n\n2. Non-Functional Requirements: \n    1. Ultra low read latency : P99 < 50ms\n    2. High availabiltiy\n    3. High read throughput.\n\n3. Back of the envelope:\n    1. 100 M active products\n    2. QPS  = 500 M daily views = 500M / 100,000 s / day = 5000 Avg QPS => Peak QPS = 3 * Avg = 15000 QPS\n    3. Write Traffic = 10M / 100,000 s/ day = 100 Avg Write QPS\n    4. Storage = Instead of Full 100M X 100M matrix only top 50 candidate items  => ~ 1KB / product\n    total storage = 100M * 1KB = 100GB => 10M orders/day * 365 * 500 bytes ~ 1.8 TB /year \n\n4. API Designing :\n     1. Recommendation : GET : /api/v1/recommendations/also-bought?item_id = ...\n    { \"source_item_id = \"..\",\n    \"startegy : \"..\",\n    \"recommendations\":[{},{},...,{}]\n    }\n \n5. Entities and Data models:\n    1. Item_co_purchase - cassandra as we need hight write throughput - and it will be kind of cold storage and it will have : source_item_id, updated_at,\ncategory_id.\n    2. Redis cluster : Hot storage\n        key : also_bought_this\n        key : recently_bought_together\n\n6.High Level Diagram: ",
      "fontSize": 12.167833438197428,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "1. Functional Requirements :\n    1. Given a product, list down ranked \"n\" no. of products to the user that are frequently bought alongside or shortly after the target product\n    2. Ingest completed order events from the upstream order service without impacting checkout latency.\n    3. Similarity scoring : process the historical purchases and real time purchases and also eliminating the generic bestsellers (e.g., carry bags, milk etc.) so that it doesn't dominate every page.\n    4. Real time post filtering : Before listing down the top list to client dynamically filter them lke out of stock, availability.\n    5. For newley launched product with zero -purchase history fall back to user already bought itmes.\n\n2. Non-Functional Requirements: \n    1. Ultra low read latency : P99 < 50ms\n    2. High availabiltiy\n    3. High read throughput.\n\n3. Back of the envelope:\n    1. 100 M active products\n    2. QPS  = 500 M daily views = 500M / 100,000 s / day = 5000 Avg QPS => Peak QPS = 3 * Avg = 15000 QPS\n    3. Write Traffic = 10M / 100,000 s/ day = 100 Avg Write QPS\n    4. Storage = Instead of Full 100M X 100M matrix only top 50 candidate items  => ~ 1KB / product\n    total storage = 100M * 1KB = 100GB => 10M orders/day * 365 * 500 bytes ~ 1.8 TB /year \n\n4. API Designing :\n     1. Recommendation : GET : /api/v1/recommendations/also-bought?item_id = ...\n    { \"source_item_id = \"..\",\n    \"startegy : \"..\",\n    \"recommendations\":[{},{},...,{}]\n    }\n \n5. Entities and Data models:\n    1. Item_co_purchase - cassandra as we need hight write throughput - and it will be kind of cold storage and it will have : source_item_id, updated_at, category_id.\n    2. Redis cluster : Hot storage\n        key : also_bought_this\n        key : recently_bought_together\n\n6.High Level Diagram: ",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
